<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>pip on Winner's Dev Notes</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/tags/pip/</link><description>Recent content in pip on Winner's Dev Notes</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 16 Mar 2019 23:20:20 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://releaseleaf.com/tags/pip/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Fix a pip Startup Traceback: Check python and Reinstall pip Safely</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/fipisttrch.html</link><pubDate>Sat, 16 Mar 2019 23:20:20 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/fipisttrch.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A pip command can fail before package installation begins when the launcher and installed pip package do not match, the environment is corrupted, or the wrong python interpreter is being used.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;img src="https://pic.imgdb.cn/item/664340940ea9cb1403bb81b5.png" alt="Example pip traceback" decoding="async" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Do not patch &lt;code&gt;site-packages/pip/__main__.py&lt;/code&gt; by hand. That only masks a particular version mismatch and will be overwritten by the next upgrade.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="confirm-the-interpreter"&gt;Confirm the interpreter&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#confirm-the-interpreter"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-1"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-2"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-2"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;python --version&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;python -m pip --version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;python -m pip&lt;/code&gt; ties pip to the selected interpreter and avoids a stale &lt;code&gt;pip&lt;/code&gt; executable elsewhere on &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fix pip install SyntaxError invalid syntax in the python Shell</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/fipiinsyin.html</link><pubDate>Sat, 16 Mar 2019 23:04:12 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/fipiinsyin.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;If typing this produces &lt;code&gt;SyntaxError: invalid syntax&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-1"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt; pip3 install ipython&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;the command was entered inside python&amp;rsquo;s interactive prompt. &lt;code&gt;pip&lt;/code&gt; is a shell command, not python syntax.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Exit the prompt with &lt;code&gt;exit()&lt;/code&gt; or the platform&amp;rsquo;s end-of-file shortcut. Then run the command in Terminal, Command Prompt, or PowerShell:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-1"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;python -m pip install ipython&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;python -m pip&lt;/code&gt; is preferable to a bare &lt;code&gt;pip3&lt;/code&gt; because it identifies which python installation will receive the package.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>